            <ArticleTitle>[Contribution of Holter monitoring in the diagnosis of a case of Prinzmetal's angina].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>177-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Prinzmetal angina is a peculiar kind of angina pectoris, in which Holter monitoring has been particularly useful for diagnosis. In this paper it is reported a 56 years old male patient with coronary artery spasm induced during coronary arteriography in which the Holter electrocardiography was of most importance for decision making.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
